libcamera: software_isp: publish manual exposure and gain controls

The software ISP set the sensor's exposure and gain itself but offered
applications no control over them: the camera's controls listed only gamma,
contrast, saturation and focus, so a camera app had no manual exposure, no
exposure compensation, and every attempt to set one was refused as invalid.
Publish ExposureTimeMode, AnalogueGainMode, AeEnable and ExposureValue from
the Agc, and ExposureTime and AnalogueGain in the sensor mode's limits at init.
A manual exposure time or gain holds while the loop keeps adjusting the other
one; switching to manual keeps the value in use until the application sets
one; the sensor then takes the values as they are, without the highlight
headroom and its digital gain. ExposureValue scales the loop's target, from -2
to +2 stops. AeState reports idle, searching or converged. Every configuration
starts again in automatic exposure at EV 0, as the other IPAs do.

